Compat before-patch for b6d536-search-budget-worker-repaired, applied to 68547f75a (the parent of
the lane commit 3d181a70c that introduced the repaired behaviour; coordinator decisions 5 and 6).

Production, declarations and neutral defaults only; no production code in this state reads any of
them, and none supplies semantic budget or bulk urgency behaviour:
- EmbeddingProvider.isAvailable() becomes a default returning true (abstract in this state). Every
  implementation in this state overrides it, so none of them changes; it lets the later test
  fixture, which implements availability() instead and reports READY, compile.
- EmbeddingProvider.availability() (a default returning READY) and the Availability record with its
  State enum and constants, the later availability snapshot the checks name.
- NoOpEmbeddingProvider.starting(), returning the existing INSTANCE, the no-op provider this
  state's checks used.
- SessionAcquireDeadlineExceededException.Phase and a (message, phase) constructor that ignores the
  phase and builds the exception exactly as this state's constructor does.
- TraceDegradation's hybrid_fallback_cause and splade_skip_cause (proto fields 7 and 8), which
  nothing in this state sets.

